# Leady Architecture Overview

Leady is an **async, multi-tenant messaging CRM**: WhatsApp/Instagram leads message a business, webhooks ingest those messages, an agent interprets a JSON flow and replies. Postgres is the source of truth; Inngest runs durable async turns.

There is no separate “ingress” product or Kubernetes Ingress layer. **Ingress = webhook API routes** that ACK quickly, persist, and enqueue work.

---

## High-level architecture

```mermaid
flowchart TB
  subgraph ingress [Ingress - Webhooks]
    WH[WhatsApp / Instagram]
    ZW["/api/webhooks/zernio"]
    MW["/api/webhooks/meta"]
    WH --> ZW & MW
  end

  subgraph persist [Postgres]
    T[Tenant + Agent config]
    L[Lead fields]
    C[Conversation flowState]
    M[Messages]
  end

  subgraph async [Inngest]
    RT[runAgentTurn]
    NU[nudgeIfSilent]
  end

  subgraph engine [Flow engine]
    INT[interpreter.ts]
    LLM[llm.ts - talk/classify/extract]
  end

  ZW & MW --> persist
  persist --> RT
  RT --> INT
  INT --> LLM
  INT --> persist
  INT --> OUT[sendOnChannel]
  OUT --> WH
```

| Layer | Location | Role |
|---|---|---|
| UI | `src/app/`, `src/components/` | Demo chat, onboarding, leads inbox, ops |
| Ingress | `src/app/api/webhooks/` | Verify signature, persist inbound, enqueue turn |
| Async jobs | `src/inngest/functions.ts` | `runAgentTurn`, `nudgeIfSilent` |
| Flow engine | `src/lib/flow/` | Types, catalog, interpreter, LLM, validation |
| CRM | `src/lib/conversations.ts`, `leads.ts`, `requests.ts` | Messages, leads, HITL, requests |
| Channels | `src/lib/channels/` | HookMyApp (Meta) and Zernio send/parse |

**Core design choice:** conversation state lives in Postgres, not in a graph framework. The “graph” is JSON on `Agent.flow`; the interpreter walks it per turn.

